       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum for ibuprofen.\n\n- **Single dose:** The usual maximum is 800 mg per dose. 1600 mg is double that.\n- **Daily dose:** The maximum for prescription use is 3,200 mg/day. Even that is rarely needed, and the dose is usually kept as low as possible. This order would give 6,400 mg/day, which carries a high risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **1600 mg/day total**, such as 400 mg four times daily\n- **800 mg three or four times daily**, which is 2,400 to 3,200 mg/day and is the usual maximum for inflammatory conditions\n- **400\u2013600 mg every 6 hours** for analgesia or antipyresis\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I'd still advise against it."
